ry":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":10815149,"width":6479,"height":3644,"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Sydney_%28AU%29%2C_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg/960px-Sydney_%28AU%29%2C_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":360,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Sydney_%28AU%29%2C_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg/1280px-Sydney_%28AU%29%2C_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail"},"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Sydney_%28AU%29%2C_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg/960px-Sydney_%28AU%29%2C_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":360,"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Sydney_%28AU%29%2C_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg/1280px-Sydney_%28AU%29%2C_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail 2x"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/Sydney_%28AU%29%2C_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sydney_(AU),_Opera_House_--_2019_--_3054.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=84651699","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Roof of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sydney_Opera_House\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Sydney Opera House\">Sydney Opera House</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sydney\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Sydney\">Sydney</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_South_Wales\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:New South Wales\">New South Wales</a>, Australia<br><small>The Sydney Opera House is one of the world\u2019s most iconic buildings and represents a unique combination of architecture, culture, and exhibition art. After initial ideas for a large opera and concert hall in Sydney were put forward in 1947, Danish architect J\u00f8rn Utzon won the international competition in 1956 with an avant-garde design whose striking sail-like shell structure accentuates Bennelong Bay. Construction was significantly delayed, causing cost overruns and political disputes. From 1959 to 1973, under a succession of planners and engineers, shell-shaped roof structures were built, which later served as railing systems and spectator areas.<br>The opening in 1973 by Queen Elizabeth II marked the beginning of a global success story as a music, opera, and festival venue. In 2007, the ensemble became a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is considered a masterpiece of modern architecture, and dominates Sydney\u2019s <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skyline\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Skyline\">skyline</a> as a symbol of cultural innovation and creative power.</small>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"Taken on\u00a025 October 2019, 11:54","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q34788025\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q34788025\"><span title=\"German photographer and mathematician\">Dietmar Rabich</span></a></bdi>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"true","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"LicenseUrl":{"value":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"commons-desc-page"}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},"438293":{"pageid":438293,"ns":6